      "clauses": [
        "Let $\\mathcal A$ be a unital complex $C^*$-algebra and let $t\\mapsto\\alpha_t$ be a strongly continuous one-parameter group of $*$-automorphisms of $\\mathcal A$. Let $\\omega$ be a $\\beta_K$-KMS state for $\\alpha$ in the physical-time convention of [[def-qsm-kms-state]], where $\\beta_K>0$ has units $\\mathrm{J}^{-1}$ and $\\hbar>0$ has units $\\mathrm{J\\,s}$. For a constant dimensionless $\\lambda>0$, define\n$$\\alpha^\\lambda_\\tau:=\\alpha_{\\tau/\\lambda},$$\nwhere $t$ and $\\tau$ are real time parameters in seconds. Then $\\omega$ is a $\\lambda\\beta_K$-KMS state for $\\alpha^\\lambda$, with strip width $\\lambda\\beta_K\\hbar$ seconds. Conversely, if $\\omega$ is a $\\widehat\\beta$-KMS state for $\\alpha^\\lambda$, then it is a $(\\widehat\\beta/\\lambda)$-KMS state for $\\alpha$.",
        "[F1] [[def-qsm-kms-state]]: a $\\beta$-KMS state for a strongly continuous automorphism group has, for every $A,B$, a bounded function continuous on $0\\le\\operatorname{Im}z\\le\\beta\\hbar$, holomorphic inside, and with boundary values $\\omega(A\\alpha_t(B))$ and $\\omega(\\alpha_t(B)A)$."
      ],
